## Desktop client

The independent Tauri application is in `client/`.

```sh
bun install --cwd client
bun run --cwd client check
bun run --cwd client test
cargo fmt --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all -- --check
cargo check --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features
cargo clippy --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-features
bun run --cwd client tauri build --bundles deb,appimage
```

The final command requires Linux WebKitGTK and related Tauri prerequisites and
emits AppImage and Debian bundles below `client/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/`.
macOS and Windows bundles require their respective native runners and are not
built by the generated workflows.
{% if client_playwright %}
Install Chromium with `bunx --cwd client playwright install chromium`, then run
`bun run --cwd client test:e2e`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
